---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Accessibility"
  description="Accessibility statement for Texas Movement Consulting: what this rebuild addressed, what's still outstanding, and how to report a barrier."
  path="/accessibility"
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">ACCESSIBILITY</div>
      <h1>Accessibility statement.</h1>
      <p>
        This page describes the current state of accessibility work on this site honestly. It is not a certification
        of compliance with any specific standard &mdash; no formal third-party audit has been performed.
      </p>

      <h2 style="margin-top: 32px;">What this rebuild addressed</h2>
      <ul class="steps" style="list-style: disc;">
        <li>A skip-to-content link at the top of every page for keyboard and screen-reader users.</li>
        <li>
          A real, keyboard-reachable mobile navigation disclosure (a button with <code>aria-expanded</code> controlling
          a visible panel) &mdash; the previous version of this site hid the entire primary navigation below 900px
          width with no replacement.
        </li>
        <li>Visible focus outlines on every interactive element (links, buttons, form controls).</li>
        <li>Descriptive alt text on every meaningful image; decorative images use empty alt text.</li>
        <li>One <code>&lt;h1&gt;</code> per page and heading levels that do not skip.</li>
        <li>Automated color-contrast and structural checks (axe-core) run against the built pages in CI.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 style="margin-top: 32px;">Known gaps</h2>
      <ul class="steps" style="list-style: disc;">
        <li>
          No manual screen-reader testing (VoiceOver, NVDA, JAWS) has been performed &mdash; only automated
          axe-core checks and manual keyboard review.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <div class="notice-panel" style="margin-top: 32px;">
        <p>
          <strong>How to report a barrier.</strong> This site does not currently have a verified contact inbox to
          route accessibility reports to (see <a href="/start">Start a diagnostic</a> for context). This is tracked as
          a launch blocker &mdash; a real reporting channel will be added here once an inbox is confirmed to exist and
          forward.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
